Subject: [PATCH] net/mlx5: support DMA-BUF scatter/gather with prompt completions

Based on the DPDK 23.11.7 release tarball.
https://fast.dpdk.org/rel/dpdk-23.11.7.tar.xz
SHA256 fa3d0380d34f8d84f2b705076bb3826823962cf141c79a1703b3acb0257ca56d

Register DMA-BUF ranges through libibverbs in the Ethernet PMD's PD.
Use the caller's CPU alias as the HCA IOVA and as the MR cache key.
Remove exact DMA-BUF ranges under the cache writer lock and invalidate
per-queue cached keys. Legacy external DMA map/unmap continues to use
ordinary verbs MRs, with cross-type overlap rejected.

Apply in the extracted source tree with git apply. On Linux, build with
Meson -Dibverbs_link=shared and link both mlx5 PMD libraries from that
build. The dlopen configuration keeps the existing mlx5 glue ABI and
its DMA-BUF map entry point reports ENOTSUP.

Let the requester opt each TX queue into signaling the last WQE of
every productive doorbell. Check completion credits before accepting
a burst so the existing CQ can handle the higher CQE rate.

